# PtolemyCatalogue.xlsx

Dataset: map-ptolemy — Ptolemy's Geography: the 6,372 coordinates of the catalogue (books 2-7) and
  the modern positions of 56 identified towns
File: data/map/ptolemy/raw/PtolemyCatalogue.xlsx
SHA-256: 448a6f229148038c5899c54d67285ce35887dedb090a7910ac46c6f61e2d2fb3 (also in
  data/map/ptolemy/inputs.lock; check with: cd data/map/ptolemy && sha256sum -c inputs.lock)
In the public repository: yes, beside this description.
Obtained: downloaded as published (fog fetch or by hand).
From: Graßhoff & Defaux, Catalog of Ptolemy's Geography (Zenodo 3585758).
URL: https://zenodo.org/api/records/3585758/files/PtolemyCatalogue.xlsx/content
Check it yourself: fog verify map-ptolemy (tools/) downloads it again into a temporary directory and
  compares it with this hash.
What could still be wrong: Five cells typed with truncated decimals (37.33333) move by less than a
  minute.
Collected: 2026-10-26
Licence: CC-BY-4.0
Sources:
- G. Graßhoff & O. Defaux, Catalog of Ptolemy's Geography, main books (Humboldt University Berlin /
  Max Planck Institute for the History of Science, 2019), after A. Stückelberger & G. Graßhoff,
  Klaudios Ptolemaios, Handbuch der Geographie (Schwabe, Basel, 2006); CC BY 4.0
  <https://zenodo.org/record/3585758>
- Wikidata, coordinate location (P625) of the modern site of each identified town, CC0; the
  identifications are those of the catalogue (column Modern_location) <https://www.wikidata.org/>
Evidence class (rule 10): model
Built by: fog build map-ptolemy
Generated files:
- src/data/presets/map-ptolemy.js
Code:
- tools/internal/build/ptolemy
- src/tabs/map/maps.js
Shown on the page:
- #tab-map/map-h2ptol
Notes: History, not evidence: the map tab carries no badge. Coordinates are rounded to 1/12 degree
  (5 minutes), Ptolemy's own finest step; five catalogue cells typed with truncated decimals
  (37.33333) move by less than a minute. modern.csv was made once with Wikidata's API (wbgetentities
  by English Wikipedia title) for 56 towns whose identification the catalogue gives and the
  literature does not dispute; Panticapaeum was left out (no coordinates under that title).

Written by `fog build explain` from data/map/ptolemy/dataset.json and data/map/ptolemy/inputs.lock: edit those, not this file.
